BuildFeatureVector — five additive inputs, read at a fixed shift
. This is the bridge between MetaTrader's market data and the ONNX graph's expected input tensor. It takes an explicit
shift
argument rather than always reading the current bar —
OnTick()
in Section 4 calls it with
shift=1
, the last fully closed bar, so a signal is never computed against a bar that can still change. Each of the five features gets a guarded computation and a fallback of exactly 0.0 rather than a divide-by-zero trap:
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| CNAMEngine::BuildFeatureVector                                   |
//| Reads indicator and price data at the given shift and writes     |
//| the five NAM inputs, in the exact FEATURE_* order the model was  |
//| trained on. shift=1 is the last closed bar; OnTick() never calls |
//| this with shift=0, so a signal is never built from a bar that    |
//| can still repaint.                                               |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
